le quorum passed to both components; BLE receives configuration ID and recovered promise.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Member count determines promise and accept quorum thresholds.','A2':'Build seeds BLE with stored promise and initializes SequencePaxos recovery.'})\nb('B-reconstruct','A6','InternalStorage::load_cache and bundled Storage implementations','Stored promise, accepted round, decided/compacted index and StopSign','Construction from supplied storage',[H,N,P,R,S],writes=['Cache loads promise and accepted round, decision and compacted index, StopSign; accepted index equals stored log length plus compacted prefix plus StopSign presence.'],existing_protections=['Storage trait requires atomic ordered operations with rollback on Err. PersistentStorage batches sync operations into one RocksDB write; MemoryStorage uses infallible in-memory updates under ordinary valid indices.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Reloaded promise constrains future prepares and accepts.','A1':'Recovered accepted history and decisions inform future promises.'})\nb('B-read-decided','A5','InternalStorage read API','Current actor-owned or synchronous storage state','read_decided_suffix/read',[H,'M-public','M-log-doc'],implementation_guards=['Suffix ends at current decided index; lower reads classify entries by absolute log index relative to decision boundary.'],external_effects=['Returns Decided entries, compacted-prefix marker, and/or StopSign status; no application state mutation.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Exposes the decided prefix rather than treating append admission as agreement.'})\nb('B-runtime-assignment','A7','ActorState pending, append_tracked, reconcile_unconfirmed and Assigned handler','EntryId-scoped pending call, assigned index and ballot','AppendNotify admission; local stable-leader append, batch reconciliation or incoming Assigned',[A,T],implementation_guards=['Stable leader (local pid and Accept phase) required for tracked leader acceptance; pending admission limited; record_assignment matches EntryId.','Batch reconciliation discards tracking on ballot mismatch.'],writes=['Allocate EntryId; retain entry until dispatch. Immediate append records accepted_after and current promise; deferred batch queues tracking intent. Remote Assigned overwrites matching pending assignment.'],external_effects=['Route TaggedProposal to leader and Assigned back to origin.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-assignment'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Assignment records acceptance position, not a quorum decision.','A2':'Records ballot at assignment but incoming Assigned has no current-ballot filter.'})\nb('B-runtime-notification','A7','ActorState::drain_notifiers','Pending call assignment and current local decided index/promise','Tick after core tick, event emission, dispatch and reconciliation',[A,T,G],reads=['Pending assigned index/ballot, current decided index and promise, wall-clock deadline'],important_branches=['If assigned idx <= decided, send Ok(idx), without testing ballot. Otherwise if assignment ballot < current promise, send Superseded; otherwise expired deadline sends Timeout; remaining calls stay pending.'],external_effects=['Oneshot completes the original append_notify future.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-assignment'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Interprets local decided boundary as completion of the identified proposal.','A2':'Checks supersession only after the success branch.'})\nb('B-runtime-drive','A7','ActorState::run and handle','Single actor owns OmniPaxos state, separate incoming/command queues and periodic timers','Executor poll, incoming message, command or timer',[A,I,J,K,Y],writes=['Serializes access; dispatches AsyncRuntime control messages separately from core protocol.'],external_effects=['Tick drives core, awaits event sends, dispatches pending work, reconciles assignments, drains notifiers and pushes subscriber data. Egress drains core messages into bounded outgoing transport channel.','handle_incoming enqueues a message; read commands obtain state after their own dispatch. Handle drop closes channels and ends actor when a receive stream closes.'],async_boundaries=['Multiple incoming messages may run between ticks; incoming handling does not itself call drain_notifiers. Event sends can await channel capacity. External transport owns routing/delivery and reconnect notification.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Drives ticks and transports protocol output, including bounded-buffer dropping of oldest messages.','A2':'Dispatches actual core Prepare and AcceptSync transitions before later notification ticks.'})\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='F-assignment',meaning='An identified pending append has a recorded assigned log index and assignment ballot, produced by a local accepted append/batch or a received Assigned message. It asserts recorded placement in that context, not decision or preservation of entry identity under later ballots.',identity={'call':'runtime EntryId within originating actor','placement':'assigned index and assignment ballot'},validity_context='Pending object until completion, failure or actor shutdown. An assignment can survive core ballot changes between notifier ticks and may be overwritten by another matching Assigned.',representation=['Pending.assigned: Option<(usize, Ballot)>'],durability='Volatile actor bookkeeping, not part of the replicated log or Storage.',recovery='No pending-call reconstruction on actor restart; channel closure returns Shutdown through handle.',source_ids=[A,T,G],unknowns=['Whether success after ballot change can refer to a different decided entry under one legal message history.']))\n# Additive knowledge answers the prior coarse boundary gap without claiming backend power-failure proof.\nm['facts'][0]['unknowns']=['PersistentStorage power-loss durability and failure rollback details remain untested; MemoryStorage has no process-crash durability.']\nm['facts'][0]['source_ids'] += [H,N,P,R]\nm['target_profile']['system_boundary']='Captured OmniPaxos core, bundled memory/persistent storage and optional async actor runtime. The actor owns tick, notification and protocol dispatch; caller owns transport delivery and application state/new-configuration startup.'\nm['target_profile']['source_ids'] += [A,I,O,H,N,P,R]\nfor a in m['activities']:\n if a['class_id']=='A4': a['realization_summary']='Validated cluster settings determine peers and shared quorum; configured peer conversion excludes local PID. StopSign identifies next cluster, which caller starts.';a['source_ids'] += [O,V,W]\n if a['class_id']=='A5': a['realization_summary']='Internal reads classify entries below the decided boundary. Actor can return suffixes or fan them to subscribers; application remains caller-owned.';a['source_ids'] += [H,A,I]\n if a['class_id']=='A6': a['realization_summary']='Construction reconstructs cached indices, rounds and StopSign from Storage. MemoryStorage retains values in-process; PersistentStorage reopens RocksDB keys and writes synchronization operations in a WriteBatch. Storage promises rollback on returned errors; detailed failure testing remains open.';a['source_ids'] += [H,N,P,R,S]\n if a['class_id']=='A7': a['realization_summary']='Synchronous append admits a proposal. Optional actor tags append_notify calls, records placement, polls decision completion on tick and exposes read/subscription APIs; transport still belongs to caller.';a['source_ids'] += [A,T,G,I]\nco=m['core_overview']; co['status']='usable';co['core_gaps']=[]\nco['rationale']='Both core paths and their ownership/reconstruction/consumption connection are traced through caller interfaces, actor dispatch and storage. Open local anomalies and backend fault details are not treated as proven protections.'\nco['formation']['explanation'] += ' InternalStorage read classifies values below the decided index; the actor has a separate proposal-identity assignment and completion layer, so correct decided-index advancement alone does not establish correct append_notify completion.'\nco['formation']['behavior_ids'] += ['B-read-decided'];co['formation']['source_ids'] += [H,A,T]\nco['context']['explanation'] += ' Build derives peers from configuration, passes quorum policy to both core components, reloads stored promise into BLE and reconstructs cached log metadata. The actor serializes protocol dispatch but can dispatch multiple incoming messages between ticks.'\nco['context']['behavior_ids'] += ['B-config-build','B-reconstruct','B-runtime-drive'];co['context']['source_ids'] += [O,V,W,H,A]\nco['connection']['explanation'] += ' Storage reconstruction supplies prior promise/history; runtime notification bookkeeping remains volatile and separate. Assigned position is consumed with a later decided-boundary read; its ballot is checked only after the success branch, leaving entry identity across replacement as a specific question.'\nco['connection']['behavior_ids'] += ['B-runtime-assignment','B-runtime-notification','B-runtime-drive','B-reconstruct'];co['connection']['fact_ids'] += ['F-assignment'];co['connection']['source_ids'] += [A,T,G,H]\nco['open_details'] += ['Pending assignment identity versus decided slot after leader replacement; existing Superseded path runs only when success condition did not match.','Actor subscriber cursor treats returned vector positions as log positions; compacted prefix markers can cover multiple indices.','PersistentStorage serialization/error rollback and crash durability remain deeper fault-contract questions.']\nfor s in m['surfaces']:\n if s['entry_point']=='OmniPaxos::handle_incoming AsyncRuntime branch':\n  s.update(disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-runtime-drive','B-runtime-assignment','B-runtime-notification'],reason='Actor dispatches runtime wire messages before the core; tick performs notification. Caller still owns transport.',source_ids=['M-public',A,I])\nm['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point='ActorState::push_to_all_subs/push_to_sub',disposition='deferred',reason='Cursor advances per returned LogEntry, while compacted prefix markers represent multiple indices; inspect snapshot subscription history and contract.',source_ids=[A,H,I],high_consequence=True))\njson.dump(m,open('runtime-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nchanges={}\nfor key in ['target_profile','A4','A5','A6','A7','core_overview','surface:OmniPaxos::handle_incoming AsyncRuntime branch','F-promise']:\n changes[key]=dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=[A,I,O,H,N,P,R,S],rationale='Resolve prior ownership and reconstruction unknowns with actual constructor, actor and backend paths; preserve the existing core mechanism and promise meaning.',preserves='No existing Candidate or Unit. Existing promise identity, guards and observation scope are unchanged; new runtime assignment is a distinct fact.')\nq=dict(disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',question='Can append_notify return Ok for an assigned slot whose entry was replaced and decided under a later ballot before the next notifier tick?',importance='Potential false client success for a write absent from the decided log, despite core consensus remaining safe.',source_ids=[A,T,G,'M-leader','M-follower','M-sync-storage'],participants=['Origin actor with pending append','Old leader','New leader and prepare/accept quorum'],objects=['EntryId','Pending.assigned','Assigned message','Decided log entry'],contexts=['One fixed configuration, non-Byzantine nodes, unbatched initial scenario','Old assignment followed by legitimate new-ballot history replacement; timers and transport explicit'],event_paths=['append_notify -> local acceptance or TaggedProposal/Assigned -> newer Prepare/AcceptSync and decision -> tick -> drain_notifiers'],activity_classes=['A7','A1','A2'],behavior_ids=['B-runtime-assignment','B-runtime-notification'],fact_ids=['F-assignment'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-runtime-drive':'Serializes actor dispatch but notifications occur only on ticks, permitting multiple protocol transitions between checks.','B-prepare':'Establishes new promise/authority.','B-formation':'Selects eligible history and forms new decision.','B-accept':'Follower synchronization can replace unchosen history.','B-sync-storage':'Installs selected suffix and decision index.','B-read-decided':'Independently observes decided entry content.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Assigned carries ballot and EntryId; batch reconciliation rejects changed-ballot tracking.','drain_notifiers sends Superseded if it sees a newer promise while the assigned index remains undecided.','New leaders must retain potentially chosen history; replacement is only legal for an entry lacking necessary quorum support.','API calls Superseded heuristic because a value may survive leadership change; successful preserved-entry completion is not itself a violation.'],unknowns=['Construct an actual emitted-message history that assigns an unchosen entry, replaces it via another quorum, and makes the slot decided before notifier evaluation, preserving per-link ordering and caller reconnect duties.','Verify public runtime test reachability and effective features for selected crate; no private-state mutation or manufactured protocol messages.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='The success branch tests idx <= decided before ballot supersession, while incoming handlers do not drain notifiers. Source reading supplies a concrete schedule discriminator. This identity obligation is stronger audit value than sparse-ID compaction or duplicate-heartbeat liveness questions; a small public-API controlled history can distinguish replacement from valid preservation without requiring crash injection.')\nsub=dict(action='continue',rationale='Complete the usable core map and select the sourced runtime assignment-consumption question, preserving supersession protections and legal-history uncertainty.',sources=sources,map_path='runtime-map.json',map_changes=changes,question=q)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-runtime.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython